$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Preparation of 1-(2-Nitrophenyl)-3-buten-1-ol (1r)6 Following the
Representative Procedure, 2-nitrobenzaldehyde (151 mg, 1.0 mmol),
RuCl3•xH2O (6.2 mg, 0.03 mmol, 0.03 equiv), allyl acetate (130 μL, 1.2
mmol, 1.2 equiv), H2O (27 μL, 1.5 mmol, 1.5 equiv), Et3N (14 μL, 0.1
mmol, 0.1 equiv), hexamethylbenzene (16 mg, 0.1 mmol, internal standard
for NMR analysis) and dioxane (2.5 mL) were combined under 30 psi of CO
at 80 °C for 24 h. Workup and purification by silica gel column
chromatography eluting with hexanes/MTBE (4:1, 400 mL) provided 1r (160
mg, 83%) as a pale yellow oil. 1-(2-Nitrophenyl)-3-buten-1-ol (1r)6,
yield 160 mg, 83%. Data for 1r: 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) 7.92 (dd, J =
8.0, 1.5, 1 H, Aryl), 7.82 (dd, J = 8.0, 2.5, 1.0, 1 H, Aryl), 7.64 (td,
J = 8.0, 1.5, 1 H, Aryl), 7.51 (td, J = 8.0, 1.5, 1 H, Aryl), 5.89 (dddd,
J = 17.0, 9.0, 7.5, 6.0, 1 H, HC(3)), 5.31 (dd, J = 8.5, 3.5, 1 H,
HC(1)), 5.22-5.17 (m, 2 H, H2C(4)), 2.72-2.67 (m, 1 H, HaC(2)), 2.50 (br,
1 H, HO), 2.45-2.38 (m, 1 H, HbC(2)). 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) 147.7
(C(2')), 139.2 (C(1')), 133.9 (C(3)), 133.4 (C(6')), 128.1 (C(3')), 128.0
(C(4')), 124.4 (C(5')), 119.0 (C(4)), 68.1 (C(1)), 42.8 (C2)). IR (NaCl)
3417 (m), 3077 (w), 2979 (w), 2915 (w), 1641 (m), 1609 (m), 1578 (m),
1523 (s), 1519 (s), 1444 (m), 1434 (m), 1347 (s), 1298 (m), 1187 (w),
1054 (m), 988 (m), 920 (m), 856(m), 821 (m) HRMS (CI) Calcd. for
C10H12NO3, 194.0817; found, 194.0815. TLC Rf 0.42 (hexanes/ethyl acetate,
3:1) [UV, CAM]
