$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Typical Procedure for Preparation of 11a and 12a. To an Et2O (10 mL)
solution of
(1Z,3E)-2-Butyl-3-ethyl-1-iodo-1,3-hexadienyl(diphenyl)-phosphine oxide
(1.0 mmol) at -78 °C was added n-BuLi (1.0 mmol). After this reaction
mixture was stirred at -78 °C for 0.5 h and quenched with 20% DCl in D2O.
(2-Butyl-3-ethyl-1-D-hexa-1,3-dienyl)-diphenyl-phosphine oxide was
obtained. If a benzaldehyde (1.2 mmol) was added to reaction mixture and
stirred for 1 h at -78 °C. Product formed after quenching with saturated
NaHCO3.
3-Butyl-2-(diphenyl-phosphinoyl)-4-ethyl-1-phenyl-hepta-2,4-dien-1-ol as
white solid, yield 387 mg, 82%. Column chromatography on silica gel
afforded pure product. Mp 162-164 °C; 1H NMR (CDCl3, Me4Si) δ 0.54-1.14
(br, 13H), 2.06-2.29 (br, 6H), 5.43 (s, 1H), 5.57 (s, 1H), 5.93-6.04 (br,
1H), 7.03-7.64 (m, 15H); 13C NMR (CDCl3, Me4Si) δ 13.3, 13.6, 14.1, 21.1,
22.6, 23.3, 29.3, 30.9 (d, 3JPC = 9.3 Hz), 75.4 (d, 2JPC = 7.4 Hz),
126.1, 126.3, 127.6, 128.1 (d, 2JPC = 12.4 Hz), 128.4 (d, 2JPC = 12.4
Hz), 129.7 (d, 1JPC = 93.3 Hz), 131.4 (d, 3JPC = 10.5 Hz), 131.5, 131.8
(d, 3JPC = 10.5 Hz), 132.2, 132.8, 135.7 (d, 1JPC = 100.1 Hz), 138.7 (d,
2JPC = 13.0 Hz), 143.5. Anal. Calcd for C31H37O2P: C, 78.78; H, 7.89.
Found: C, 78.62; H, 8.01. HRMS calcd for C31H37O2P 472.2531, found
472.2546.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, Wittig-Horner elimination, product formation depends on
reaction time
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Preparation of Vinyl Allenes from 1-Lithio-1,3-dienyl Phosphine Oxides
and Aldehydes by the Wittig-Horner Reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Xi, Zhenfeng; Zhang, Wen-Xiong; Song, Zhiyi; Zheng, Weixin; Kong, Fanzhi;
Takahashi, Tamotsu
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2005), 70(22), 8785-8789

