$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1-(2'-Furyl)-2-(trimethylsilyl)-ethanol. Magnesium turnings (10.1 g, 415
mmol) were placed in a 1 L 3-neck flask. A condenser and a pressure
equalizing addition funnel were attached. The apparatus was flame dried
and flushed with nitrogen gas (3 ×). Chloromethyltrimethylsilane (42.4 g,
346 mmol) and ether (200 mL) were slowly added to the dry magnesium.
After the addition was complete, the solution was refluxed for 1 h.
Freshly distilled furfural (25 mL, 300 mmol) and dry ether (300 mL) were
slowly added to the Grignard reagent at 0 °C and the solution was stirred
for 12 h. The reaction was quenched with satd aq NH4Cl (200 mL) and was
extracted with ether (3 × 100 mL). The organic layer was washed with satd
aq NaHCO3 (2 × 50 mL), brine (2 × 50 mL), dried (Na2SO4), and
concentrated under reduced pressure to give a yellow oil (not shown in
the paper), (50.05 g, 272 mmol, 90% yield).
1-(2'-Furyl)-2-(trimethylsilyl)-ethanol, yield 50.05 g, 272 mmol, 90% Rf
0.58 (ether/hexane = 3:7); 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3 ) δ 7.28 (dd, J = 0.7,
1.8 Hz, 1H), 6.24 (dd, J = 1.8, 3.1 Hz, 1H), 6.13 (d, J = 3.3 Hz, 1H),
4.77 (dd, J = 6.9, 8.8 Hz, 1H), 3.13 (bs, 1H), 1.28 (dd, J = 14.1, 8.8
Hz, 1H), 1.23 (dd, J = 14.1, 6.8 Hz, 1H), -0.10 (s, 9H); 13C NMR (75 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 157.7, 141.6, 110.1, 105.5, 65.6, 24.8, -1.4; IR (thin film)
3390, 2950, 2895, 1655, 1505, 1250, 1010, 860, 690 cm-1; HRMS (CI, NH3)
accurate mass cald for (C9H16O2Si)+ requires m/z 184.0919, found m/z
184.0905.
