$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure B- Synthesis of
(Z)-1,5-syn-diols: 2-Allenyl-4,4,5,5-tetraphenyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolane4 (1
equiv) and (Ipc)2BH5 (1 equiv) were weighed out in a glove box. The
crystalline (Ipc)2BH was ground with a glass rod, then removed from the
glove box and dissolved in CH2Cl2 (0.5 M). The solution was cooled to 0
°C and a solution of the aforementioned allene in CH2Cl2 (0.5M) was added
dropwise via cannula. The mixture was stirred for 2 h at 0 °C, then was
cooled to -78°C and a solution of the first aldehyde (0.8 equiv) was
added dropwise. The mixture was stirred for 3 h at -78 °C, then the
second aldehyde (2.0 equiv) was added. The mixture was allowed to warm to
ambient temperature and stirred for an additional 15-64 h. Ethanolamine
was added and the solution was stirred for 2 h, followed by dilution with
CH2Cl2 and brine. The aqueous phase was extracted with CH2Cl2 (2X), dried
over Na2SO4, filtered, and concentrated in vacuo. The products were
separated by flash chromatography in the usual manner.
(1S,5S,Z)-1-(4-nitrophenyl)-7-phenylhept-3-ene-1,5-diol (16). A solution
of 2-allenyl-4,4,5,5- tetraphenyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolane4 (103 mg, 0.25
mmol) and (lIpc)2BH5 (72 mg, 0.25 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (2 mL) was treated with
aldehyde SI-38 (108 mg, 0.20 mmol, 0.4 M in CH2Cl2) and second aldehyde
SI-48 (184 mg, 0.38 mmol) according to General Procedure B. The reaction
was worked-up by addition of methanol (2 mL) in place of ethanolamine and
the resulting solution was stirred for 4 h. The solution was concentrated
in vacuo. The resulting oil was purified by flash column chromatography
(10% to 20% to 25% EtOAc-hexanes) to give the title Compound as a 12:1
mixture of diastereomers (141 mg, 65%). An analytical sample was acquired
by preparative HPLC (30% EtOAc-hexanes). Data for
(1S,5S,Z)-1-(4-nitrophenyl)-7-phenylhept-3-ene-1,5-diol (16): [α]D23 =
-146.1 (c 1.01, CHCl3);ee 90%; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.18 (d, J = 8.4
Hz, 2H) 7.47 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 2H), 7.28 (t, J = 6.8 Hz, 2H), 7.22-7.16 (m,
3H), 5.67 (t, J = 10 Hz, 1H), 5.37 (q, J = 8.4 Hz, 1H), 4.94 (t, J =5.2
Hz, 1H), 4.36 (q, J = 6.8 Hz, 1H), 3.24 (br s, 1H), 2.74-2.60 (m, 3H),
2.52-2.33 (m, 2H),1.96-1.87 (m, 1H), 1.81-1.73 (m, 1H); 13C NMR (400 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 151.1, 147.2, 141.6, 136.5, 128.5, 128.4, 126.6, 126.4, 126.0,
123.5, 71.6, 66.6, 38.6, 36.6, 31.6; IR (thin film) 3367,2926, 1519, 1346
cm-1; HRMS (ESI) calcd for C19H21NO4Na 350.1363 m/z; observed 350.1369
m/z
