$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 9-(tert-Butyl-diphenyl-silanyloxy)-3,7-dimethyl-1-phenyl-nona-3,7-dien-1-ol
(3) In a sealed vial were added the stannane 1 (9:1 mixture) (0.10g, 0.18
mmol) and benzaldehyde (0.021 g, 0.2 mmol, 1.1 equiv) and were stirred
until the mixture became homogeneous. The reaction was heated in a
sandbath for one day, until a strong spot was detected by TLC (9/1
Hexanes/Ethyl Acetate as solvent, rf = 0.36). Neat mixture was directly
purified by flash column chromatography (9/1, hexanes/ethyl acetate as
eluent) to give 0.060 mg of a thick oil in an 85% yield in respect to the
secondary stannane. No products expected from the reaction of the primary
stannane were observed. The product is >95% one isomer based on both 1H
NMR and 13C NMR spectroscopy. Stereochemistry of the coupling product 3
was determined by nOe experiments. Strong enhancement was observed
between protons Ha and Hb (11.7 %) and to lesser extent between protons
Hb and Hc (2.4 %).
9-(tert-Butyl-diphenyl-silanyloxy)-3,7-dimethyl-1-phenyl-nona-3,7-dien-1-ol
(3), yield 0.060 mg, 85% 1H NMR δ (CDCl3): 1.08 (s, 9 H), 1.44 (s, 3 H),
1.93-2.12 (m, 3 H), 2.33 (dd, J = 13.5 Hz, 5.4 Hz, 1 H), 2.64 (dd, J =
13.8 Hz, 9.0 Hz, 1 H), 4.24 (d, J = 6.4 Hz, 1 H), 4.81 (dd, J = 8.4 Hz,
4.8 Hz, 1 H), 5.33-5.40 (m, 2 H), 7.21-7.55 (m, 10 H), 7.65-7.81 (m, 5 H)
13C NMR δ (CDCl3): 17.0, 19.9, 24.4, 26.9, 27.5, 40.1, 43.1, 61.7, 72.6,
124.8, 126.2, 127.9, 128.0, 128.8, 129.4, 129.9, 131.7, 134.4, 136.0,
137.0, 144.7, FTIR (neat) 3538, 2931, 1428, 1112, 910 cm-1 HRMS (FAB) m/z
= 521.2831 [521.2852 calcd for C33H42O2Si+Na].
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, no solvent
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A Study of Oligoprenyl Coupling Reactions with Allylic Stannanes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Radetich, Branko; Corey, E. J.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2002), 4(20), 3463-3464

