$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure 1: synthesis of allylic and
homoallylic alcohols. Neat aldehyde (5 mmol, 1 equiv) was added dropwise
via syringe to a flask containing a THF solution (12 mL) of
isopropenylmagnesium bromide (6 mmol, 1.2 equiv) at 0°C. The resulting
solution was allowed to stir at this temperature for 5 minutes before
being warmed to room temperature, at which it was stirred for 15 minutes.
The reaction was promptly quenched with saturated ammonium chloride (10
mL), and extracted with diethyl ether (3 x 25 mL). The combined organic
layers were sequentially washed with saturated aqueous sodium bicarbonate
(10 mL) and brine (15 mL), dried over anhydrous Na2SO4, filtered, and
concentrated under light vacuum. The crude allylic alcohols were either
used without further purification, or purified on Si gel using a
EtOAc:pentanes mobile phase.
(±)-2-methyl-1-(2-(trifluoromethyl)phenyl)prop-2-en-1-ol - Synthesized
using general procedure 1. The crude allylic alcohol was sufficiently
pure after work up, and was afforded as a white semi-solid (0.980 g, 4.55
mmol, 91%) upon concentration. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.69-7.64 (m,
2H), 7.56 (ddd, J = 7.8, 1.1, 0.6 Hz, 1H), 7.42-7.37 (m, 1H), 5.51 (s,
1H), 5.23 (dq, J = 2.4, 0.8 Hz, 1H), 5.06-5.03 (m, 1H), 2.22 (s, 1H),
1.60 (s, 2H). 13C NMR(100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 145.64 (s), 140.58 (s), 132.23
(d, J = 1.1 Hz), 128.63 (s), 127.88 (s), 125.71 (s), 125.50 (q, J = 5.8
Hz), 122.98 (s), 111.29 (s), 71.85 (q, J = 2.4 Hz), 19.53 (s). 19F
NMR(376 MHz, CDCl3) δ -57.74 (s). IR (cm-1, thin film) 3335, 3080, 2970,
2920, 1456, 1311, 1240, 1159, 1124, 1112, 1033, 908, 769. HRMS (ESI+):
Calc'd for C11H15FNO, 234.11057; found, 234.11104. MP 32-34 °C.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM no time given for warming to room temperature
