$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for Z-enynols formation: To
a solution of vinylic tellurides (1a-d) (1mmol) in THF (6 mL) at -78°C
under Ar, n-butyllithium (1.1 mmol) was added at once and the reaction
stirred for 15 min. The aldehyde or ketone was added and the reaction
stirred for 1 hour. The cooling bath was removed and the mixture treated
with saturated solution of ammonium chloride (5 mL), diluted with ethyl
acetate (15 mL). After drying the organic phase (MgSO4), the solvent was
removed under vacuum and the residue purified by flash chromatography on
silica gel using hexane:acetate (80:20) as eluent.
(Z)-1-(4-methoxyphenyl)-2,5-diphenylpent-2-en-4-yn-1-ol (3w). Yield:
0.289g (85%). The product 3w was easy purified by column chromatography
however, was unstable to obtain reliable elemental analyses. 1H NMR
(CDCl3, 400 MHz), δ (ppm): 7.43-7.39 (m, 4H), 7.29-7.27 (m, 5H),
7.22-7.20 (m, 3H), 6.84 (d, J = 8.7 Hz, 2H), 6.36 (s, 1H), 6.12 (s, 1H),
3.73 (s, 3H), 2.73 (s, 1H). 13C NMR (CDCl3, 100 MHz) δ (ppm): 158.68,
154.24, 137.88, 133.99, 131.40, 128.38, 128.30, 128.15, 128.13, 127.58,
126.88, 122.94, 113.71, 109.32, 96.24, 86.59, 73.36, 55.10. MS (relative
intensity) m/z: 340 (100), 324 (19), 135 (75), 77 (29).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
