$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM To a round-bottom flask were added THF (22 mL) and diisopropylamine (844
μL 6.6 mmol), and the mixture was cooled to 78 °C. n-BuLi (2.5 M in
hexanes, 6.6 mmol) was added slowly, and the mixture was stirred for 15
min. Ethyl acetate (586 μL, 6.0 mmol) was then added dropwise, and the
solution was stirred for 50 min. (E)-3-(2-Fluorophenyl)-acrylaldehyde
(3d) (6.0 mmol) was added dropwise and stirred for 10 min. The reaction
was quenched by the addition of sat'd. aq. NH4Cl (1.7 mL), followed by
immediate transfer to a separatory funnel containing diethyl ether (25
mL). The mixture was extracted with diethyl ether (25 mL), washed with
brine (2 x 25 mL) and water (2 x 25 mL), and dried over MgSO4. Removal of
solvent yielded the corresponding hydroxyester in >99% yield. No further
purification was needed before the oxidation with Jones' Reagent. Yield
99%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A General Organocatalyzed Michael-Michael Cascade Reaction Generates
Functionalized Cyclohexenes
