$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
1-((Z)-2-Phenylethynyl-1-cyclooctenyl)-3-buten-1-ol (6a); Following the
General Procedure E; General Procedure E. To a stirred solution of 11
(4.50 mmol) in Et2O (25 ml) was added allyl Grignard reagent (0.81 M
solution in Et2O, 9.00 mmol) at 0 °C and stirred for 30 min. The mixture
was then quenched by addition of saturated aq. NH4Cl, extracted with
EtOAc three times, and washed with brine. The organic layers were dried
over Na2SO4 and concentrated under reduced pressure. The residue was
purified by silica gel column chromatography to give 6.
(E)-6-Benzyloxymethyl-3-methyl-8-phenyl-1,5-octadien-7-yn-4-ol (6n);
Following the General Procedure E; the reaction was carried out in THF;
purified by silica gel column chromatography (hexane/EtOAc = 3/1)
(Diastereomeric mixture: 98% yield, colorless oil). The following data
are for a mixture of two diastereomers (0.5/0.5);. 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ 1.08
(d, J= 7.0 Hz, 1.5H), 1.11 (d, J= 7.0 Hz, 1.5H), 1.93 (br s, 0.5H), 1.99
(br s, 0.5H), 2.37 (sextet, J= 7.0 Hz, 0.5H), 2.54 (sextet, J= 7.0 Hz,
0.5H), 4.13 (t, J= 1.2 Hz, 1.0H), 4.15 (t, J= 1.5 Hz, 1.0H), 4.53-4.62
(m, 0.5H), 4.58 (d, J= 1.8 Hz, 1.0H), 4.59 (d, J= 2.1 Hz, 1.0H), 4.68 (t,
J= 7.1 Hz, 0.5H), 5.11-5.19 (m, 2.0H), 5.81-5.89 (m, 1.0H), 6.02 (q, J=
1.2 Hz, 0.5H), 6.03 (q, J= 1.5 Hz, 0.5H), 7.27-7.46 (m, 10.0H); 13C NMR
(CDCl3) δ 14.90, 16.07, 43.76, 44.49, 72.04, 72.09, 72.12, 73.42, 85.33,
95.29, 95.47, 116.57, 122.51, 122.86, 122.89, 127.70, 127.75, 128.33,
128.38, 128.49, 131.53, 138.01, 138.54, 139.75, 140.12; HRMS (FAB) calcd
for C23H23O (M+-OH) 315.1749, found 315.1755.
