$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Methyl 3-hydroxy-2-methylene-3-(4-pyridinyl)propanoate (18b).
Purification by column chromatography (5:1 hexane/EtOAc) afforded a
desired compound 18b (181 mg, 93%) as an ivory crystal. Spectral data
were identical to those previously reported.2 TLC: R f 0.22 (1:5
hexane/EtOAc). mp: 129.5 °C (Lit.,3 : 143-144 °C (from EtOH)). 1H-NMR
(400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 8.54 (d, 2H, J = 6.4 Hz), 7.32 (d, 2H, J = 6.4 Hz),
6.39 (s, 1H), 5.87 (s, 1H), 5.52 (s, 1H), 3.74 (s, 3H). 13C-NMR (100 MHz,
CDCl3): δ 166.6, 150.8, 149.9, 141.1, 127.4, 121.6, 72.4, 52.4. LRMS
(FAB) m/z (rel int): 194 ([M], 35). HRMS m/z calcd for C10H12NO3 194.0817
found 194.0813.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Baylis-Hillman reaction, 1-butyl-3-methyltriazolium triflimide as solvent
gave lower yield
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of 1,3-Dialkyl-1,2,3-triazolium Ionic Liquids and Their
