$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure A: Grignard Addition to an
Aldehyde: Grignard Reagent (2.0 eq.) was added dropwise to a stirred
solution of aldehyde (1.0 eq.) in THF (10 mL per 1.00 mmol substrate) at
-30 °C and the resulting solution was stirred at this temperature for 3
h. A saturated, aqueous solution of NH4Cl was added and the aqueous phase
was extracted with ethyl acetate (3 x 30 mL). The combined organic
extracts were washed with brine (30 mL), dried over MgSO4, filtered and
concentrated to give the crude product, which was then purified as
specified. 1-(4-Methoxypyridin-2-yl)prop-2-en-1-ol, 9 as an oil, yield
0.421 g, 2.55 mmol, 71%. Rf 0.29 (ethyl acetate); IR νmax (thin
film/cm-1) 3205 (O-H), 1593 (C=C); 1H NMR δH (400 MHz, CDCl3) 8.36 (1 H,
d, J 5.8, NCH), 6.81 (1 H, d, J 2.5, C(CHOH)CH), 6.75 (1 H, dd, J 5.8,
2.5, NCHCH), 5.97 (1 H, ddd, J 17.0, 10.2, 6.7, CH=CH2), 5.46 (1 H, d, J
17.0, trans- CH=CHH), 5.25 (1 H, d, J 10.2, cis-CH=CHH), 5.13 (1 H, d, J
6.7, CHOH), 3.86 (3 H, s, OCH3), 3.61 (1 H, br s, OH); 13C NMR δC (100
MHz, CDCl3) 166.5 (COMe), 162.0 (CCHOH), 149.2 (NCH), 139.4 (CH=CH2),
116.5 (CH=CH2), 109.3 (NCHCH), 106.2 (C(CHOH)CH), 74.3 (CHOH), 55.2
(OCH3); MS m/z (ESI+) 166 (10%, M+H+), 188 (65%, M+Na+), 353 (100%,
2M+Na+); HRMS (ESI+) C9H11NO2 requires M+H+ 166.0863, found 166.0864
(-1.0 ppm).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Intramolecular Hydride Addition to Pyridinium Salts: New Routes to
