dilution and cooling to 0 °C benzaldehyde (0.1 mL, 1.0 mmol) was added
and the reaction mixture was stirred at this temperature for 1 h. After
quenching with triethanolamine (0.15 mL, 1.1 mmol), work up and
purification by flash column chromatography (silica gel, pentane/diethyl
ether 2:1) the desired product 4d was obtained.The dr was determined with
the signals at 6.99 and 6.67 ppm. A colorless oil (248 mg, 0.82 mmol,
82%, dr 93:7). 1H NMR (CDCl3, 300 MHz): δ = 7.38-7.28 (m, 5H), 6.99 (dt,
J = 15.6, 7.3 Hz, 1H), 5.88 (dt, J = 15.5, 1.5 Hz, 1H), 5.10 (s, 1H),
5.00 (s, 1H), 4.47 (dd, J = 8.7, 2.6 Hz, 1H), 4.14 (t, J = 6.6 Hz, 2H),
2.94 (d, J = 7.2 Hz, 2H), 2.57-2.47 (m, 1H), 2.17 (d, J = 2.6 Hz, 1H),
1.70-1.60 (m, 2H), 1.47-1.34 (m, 2H), 0.94 (t, J = 7.4 Hz, 3H), 0.85 (d,
J = 7.2 Hz, 3H). 13C NMR (CDCl3, 75 MHz): δ = 166.4, 148.4, 146.0, 142.5,
128.3, 127.8, 126.8, 123.2, 113.9, 77.1, 64.2, 48.7, 36.6, 30.7, 19.2,
16.7, 13.7. IR (film, cm-1): 3481, 3064, 3030, 2962, 2934, 2875, 1719,
1654, 1494, 1455, 1386, 1312, 1277, 1203, 1163, 1066, 1025, 988, 904,
840, 761, 734, 702. HRMS (ESI): calculated for C19H26O3Na: m/z =
325.1774; found m/z = 325.1773.
