$DATUM (Z)-1,2-Diphenyl-1-hydroxy-3-trifluoromethylhept-2-ene (4b). A solution
of enol ether 3 (220 mg, 1 mmol), n-butyllithium (1.3 mL of a 1.6 M
solution in hexanes, 2.1 mmol), and TMEDA (490 mg, 2.1 mmol) in hexane
(10 mL), after addition of benzaldehyde (132 mg, 1.2 mmol), afforded,
after workup and purification, the alcohol 4b (238 mg, 83%). IR (neat)
3450, 1674 cm-1; 19F NMR δ - 54.9 (s); 1H NMR δ 0.7 (t, J = 7.4 Hz, 3 H),
1.1 (qt, J = 7.4 Hz, 2 H), 1.35 (m, 2 H), 1.9 (t, J = 7.3 Hz, 2 H), 6.1
(s, CHOH), 6.7 (s, OH), 7.2 (m, 10 H); 13C RMN δ 13.6, 22.7, 29.7, 31.5,
71.6 (q, 4 JCF= 2.7 Hz), 126.0 (q, 1 JCF= 278 Hz, CF3), 126.2, 127.2,
127.5, 127.7, 128.1, 128.4, 129.0, 129.6 (q, 2 JCF = 27 Hz, CF3-C═C),
135.4, 140.6, 148.8 (q, 3 JCF = 5 Hz; Anal. Calcd for C20H21F3O:C, 71.86;
H, 6.29. Found: C, 71.27; H, 6.58.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
