$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Triethyl-hex-5-en-3-ynyloxy-sliane: To a
stirred solution of vinyl bromide (1.0 M solution of THF, 18 mL, 18.0
mmol), Pd(PPh3)4 (208 mg, 0.18 mmol), CuI (91.6 mg, 0.48 mmol), and Et3N
(3.4 mL, 24.0 mmol) was added a solution of but-3-ynyloxy-triethylsilane
(2.21 g, 12.0 mmol) in THF (6 mL) via a syringe pump over 1 hour. The
reaction mixture was stirred at room temperature for 3 hours and then it
was filtered through Celite. The solvent was removed in vacuo.
Purification of residue by flash chromatography (SiO2: Rf = 0.72,
hexanes/EtOAc = 20/1) gave the enyne product.
2-Hydroxy-3-thiophen-2-yl-hexa-3,5-dienoic acid ethyl ester, yield 72%.
1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): 7.32 (dd, J = 4.8, 1.2 Hz, 1H), 7.00 (m, 2H),
6.62 (ddd, J = 10.1, 10.8, 16.8 Hz, 1H), 6.47 (d, J = 10.8 Hz, 1H), 5.45
(dd, J = 16.8, 1.2 Hz, 1H), 5.25 (dd, J = 10.1, 1.2 Hz, 1H), 4.83 (d, J =
5.4 Hz, 1H), 4.17 (m, 2H), 3.38 (d, J = 5.4 Hz, 1H), 1.17 (t, J = 7.2 Hz,
3H). 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3): 172.9, 136.4, 134.0, 133.2, 131.9, 128.0,
126.7, 126.3, 121.2, 75.8, 62.2, 13.9. HRMS Calcd. for C12H15O3S (M+1):
239.0742, Found: 239.0738.FTIR (neat): 3479, 2980, 1732, 1441, 1212,
1094, 915, 703 cm-1.HPLC (Chiralcel OD-H column, 2% i-PrOH/hexanes, 0.5
mL/min, 254 nm), tmajor = 22.9 min, tminor = 27.6 min; ee = 92%.[α]D = +
118.6 (c = 2.49, CH2Cl2).
