$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for TiIII-Mediated
Barbier-type Crotylation of Carbonyl Compounds. Strictly deoxygenated THF
(20 mL) was added to a mixture of Cp2TiCl2 (2.5 mmol) and Mn dust (8
mmol) under an Ar atmosphere, and the suspension was stirred at room
temperature until it turned lime green (after about 15 min). A solution
of carbonyl compound (1 mmol), allylic halide (2 mmol), and LiBr (1.5
mmol when indicated) in THF (1 mL) was then added dropwise for 5 min, and
the mixture was stirred for a further 6 h at room temperature, 0 °C, or
-20 °C (when indicated). The reaction was quenched with brine and
extracted with EtOAc. The organic layer was washed with brine and dried
(anhyd Na2SO4) and the solvent removed. Products 4, 6, and 18-28 were
purified by flash chromatography on silica gel (hexane/EtOAc) and
characterized by spectroscopic techniques.27 The yields are listed in
Tables 1 and 2. 21: (99 mg, 72%), 1:4 mixture of syn:anti isomers,
colorless oil. 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 5.85-5.73 (m, 1H), 5.19-5.11 (m,
2H), 3.94 (d, J = 9.9 Hz, 1H), 2.90-2.73 (m, 1H), 1.99-1.90 (m, 2H), 1.81
(s, 3H), 1.73-1.32 (m, 4H), 1.17 (d, J = 6.5 Hz, 3H), 1.06 (m, 3H), 0.94
(s, 3H), 0.90 (s, 3H). 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ 143.3 (CH,antiisomer),
141.7 (CH, syn isomer), 139.2 (C, syn isomer), 137.3 (C, anti isomer)
133.3 (C, anti isomer), 132.5 (C, syn isomer), 115.8 (CH2, anti isomer),
113.3 (CH2, syn isomer), 75.4 (CH, syn isomer), 73.7 (CH, anti isom),
44.3 (CH, anti isomer), 43.0 (CH, syn isomer), 40.4 (CH2), 40.2 (CH2, syn
isomer), 34.9 (C, anti isomer), 34.8 (C, syn isomer), 34.6 (CH2, anti
isomer), 34.4 (CH2, syn isomer), 29.1 (CH3, anti isomer), 28.9 (CH3, syn
isomer), 21.5 (CH3, syn isomer), 21.3 (CH3, anti isomer), 19.5 (CH2, anti
isomer), 19.4 (CH2, syn isomer), 17.8 (CH3, anti isomer), 17.3 (CH3, syn
isomer). HRMS FAB m/z calcd for C14H24ONa [M+Na]+: 231.1725; found:
231.1719.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, stereoselective, Barbier-type crotylation
