$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Representative Procedure I: Preparation of
(4S,5S)-5-Hydroxy-4-methyl-5-phenyl-3-pentanone (16a) 6 Phosphoramide 2
(55 mg, 0.15 mmol, 0.15 equiv) was dried under vacuum (0.05 mmHg) for 12
at rt. Dichloromethane (2 mL) was added and the solution was cooled to
-78 °C. (Z)-5 (1/15, E/Z) (203 mg, 1.1 mmol, 1.1 equiv) was added
dropwise. The solution was allowed to equilibrate for a few minutes
before benzaldehyde (102 μL, 1.0 mmol) was added dropwise via syringe.
The reaction mixture was stirred at -78 °C for 8 h, then quickly poured
into a rapidly stirring mixture of saturated, aqueous NaHCO3 and CH2Cl2
at 0 °C and allowed to continue stirring overnight. The two-phase mixture
was filtered through Celite, then the phases were separated, and the
aqueous phase was extracted with CH2Cl2 (3 x 10 mL). The organic phases
were combined, washed with brine (5 mL), then dried over Na2SO4, filtered
and concentrated in vacuo. The crude material was purified by column
chromatography (SiO2, pentane/Et2O, 6/1). Preparation of
(4S,5S)-5-Hydroxy-4-methyl-5-(2'-furyl)-3-pentanone (16c) 8
2-Furfuraldehyde (88 μL, 1.0 mmol) was added to a solution of (Z)-5 and
(S,S)-2 and allowed to stir at -78 °C for 8 h. The reaction mixture was
quenched in a mixture of NaHCO3 and CH2Cl2. Filtration through Celite,
followed by extraction with CH2Cl2 (3x10 mL) afforded the crude product
which was purified by column chromatography (SiO2, pentane/Et2O, 6/1) to
give 144 mg (80%) of 16c as a clear, pale, yellow oil. Analytical data
for 16c: 1H NMR: (CDCl3, 500 MHz) 7.34 (d, J =1.7, 1 H, HC(4'')); 6.30
(dd, J = 3.2, 1.7, 1 H, HC(3'')); 6.25 (d, J = 3.2, 1 H, HC(2''); 5.65
(br s, 1 H, HC(5), syn); 3.30 (d, J = 1.9, 1 H, OH); 3.07, (dq, J = 7.1,
2.8, 1 H, HC(4)); 2.64 (q, J = 7.0, 2 H, HC(2)); 1.21 (t, J = 7.0, 3 H,
H3C(1)); 0.99 (d, J = 7.1, 3 H, H3C(1')) 13C NMR: (CDCl3, 125 MHz) 215.59
(C(3)); 154.58 (C(1'')); 141.65 (C(4'')); 110.25 (C(3'')); 106.62
(C(2'')); 69.36 (C(2)); 50.27 (C(5)); 34.74 (C(4)); 16.90 (C(1)); 8.35
(C(1')) TLC: Rf 0.20 (pentane/Et2O, 6/1, anisaldehyde) SFC: syn-16c: t
R(4R,5R) 2.1 min (16.7%); t R(4S,5S) 2.4 min (83.3%) (Daicel Chiralcel
OD, 5% MeOH in CO2, 150 bar, 40 °C, 3.0 mL min-1)
