$DATUM 7732-18-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Procedure for diastereoselective Henry
reaction promoted by per-6-ABCD (1) Per-6-ABCD 1, (0.112 g, 0.1 mmol) was
suspended in ACN:water (1:1, v/v) (3 mL). Aldehyde 2 (0.02 g, 0.1 mmol)
dissolved in acetone (0.5 mL) was added dropwise to 1 with constant
stirring and continued for an hour to complete complexation. Then
nitroethane 5 (0.005 mL, 0.1 mmol) was added and allowed to stir at -20
°C for 7 h. After completion of the reaction, products were extracted
with ethyl acetate, dried with sodium sulphate and concentrated under
reduced pressure. The resulting crude product was purified by passing
over a column of siliga gel 60-120 mesh using pet-ether/ethyl acetate
(7/3 ratio as an eluent) affording Henry product 6a-j as a light
yellow-dark yellow viscous oil liquid which was analyzed by NMR
spectroscopy (300 MHz, CDCl3, T = 300 K, TMS = 0 ppm), ESI-MS and
CSP(Chiral Stationary Phase)-HPLC. Percentage ee was determined by HPLC
at 254 nm using chiralcel OD-H column, with n-hexane and i-propanol
mixture at a flow rate 0.5-1.0 mL/min (or it otherwise noted). After
extraction of the product, per-6-ABCD (1) is washed thrice with ethyl
acetate, filtered, dried in vacuum and reused.
2-nitro-1-(thiophen-2-yl)propan-1-ol (Table 4, Entry 9): Compound 6i was
prepared according to the general procedure and purified by column
chromatography (petether/ ethyl acetate = 8/2) to give a yellow liquid
(98% yield). 1H-NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3, δ ppm): 1.24 (d, J = 6.8 Hz,
3H)(syn), 1.42 (d, J = 6.8 Hz, 0.06H)(anti), 2.78 (br s, 1H)(syn), 2.84
(br s, 0.02H)(anti), 4.80 (dd, J = 4.8, 7.0 Hz, 0.02H)(anti), 4.91 (dd, J
= 8.8, 6.8 Hz, 1H)(syn), 4.98 (d, J = 9.1 Hz, 1H)(syn), 5.21 (d, J = 4.8
Hz, 0.02H)(anti), 7.96 (m, 3.07H)(syn/anti). 13C-NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3, δ
ppm): 12.1 (anti), 14.0 (syn), 74.1 (anti), 76.0 (syn), 84.9 (anti), 86.1
(syn), 117.6 (anti), 118.6 (syn), 125.4 (syn), 125.9 (anti), 129.0
(anti), 129.8 (syn), 148.7 (syn), 149.4 (anti). ESI-MS: m/z Calcd. for
C7H9NO3S [M+H]+ : 188.0381; Found, 188.0391 (Rel. Int.100%). HPLC: The
diastereomeric ratios (dr) (syn/anti) and enantiomeric excess was
determined by HPLC with a Chiralcel OD-H column (90:10
n-hexane-isopropanol, 0.5 mL/min, 254 nm); as a mixture of syn/anti
(98:2), 88% and 80% ee respectively; Anti: major enantiomer tmajor = 19.7
min, minor enantiomer tminor = 20.9 min; Syn: major enantiomer tmajor =
23.4 min, minor enantiomer tminor = 26.5 min.
