$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Alkyl iodide 18 (1 equiv) was stirred in 3:2
pentane / ether to give a 0.1 M solution. The solution was cooled to -78
°C and a 1.8 M tert-butyllithium solution in pentane (2.2 equiv) was
added by a syringe. After 10-15 min at -78 °C, the appropriate
β,®-unsaturated aldehyde (1.3- 1.8 equiv) was added by a syringe. Once
TLC analysis indicated conversion to allylic alcohol (ca. 1 h) the
reaction was quenched with sat. NaHCO3 and allowed to warm to 23 °C. The
resulting mixture was extracted with ether. The combined extracts were
washed with brine, dried (MgSO4), filtered, and concentrated to give the
corresponding allylic alcohol.
(E)-1-(syn-7-Allylnorborn-2-en-7-yl)-4-phenylbut-3-en-2-ol (19c).Yield
288 mg, 94% TLC Rf = 0.48, (3:1 hexanes / ethyl acetate); 1H NMR (500
MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.39 (dd, J = 8.9, 1.7 Hz, 2H), 7.33 (dd, J = 8.9, 7.3 Hz,
2H), 7.25 (dd, J = 7.3, 1.7 Hz, 1H), 6.56 (d, J = 15.7 Hz, 1H), 6.24 (dd,
J = 15.7, 7.0 Hz, 1H), 5.98-5.90 (m, 2H), 5.80-5.68 (m, 1H), 5.04-4.96
(m, 2H), 4.54-4.46 (m, 1H), 2.60 (br dd, J = 3.3, 3.3 Hz, 1H), 2.47 (br
dd, J = 3.3, 3.3 Hz, 1H), 2.42 (dd, J = 14.7, 6.6 Hz, 1H), 2.35 (dd, J =
14.7, 7.7 Hz, 1H), 1.93-1.89 (m, 1H), 1.83-1.78 (m, 1H), 1.67 (dd, J =
14.7, 7.3 Hz, 1H), 1.57 (dd, J = 14.7, 5.1 Hz, 1H), 1.47 (d, J = 3.7 Hz,
1H), 0.99-0.92 (m, 2H); 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ 137.7, 136.7, 134.5,
134.0, 133.4, 129.7, 128.6, 127.7, 126.4, 115.7, 71.2, 60.6, 48.2, 47.7,
37.9, 34.1, 23.24, 23.16; IR (film) 3382, 3058, 3025, 2960, 2879, 1636,
1493, 1447, 1329, 967 cm-1. HRMS (CI+ w/CH4) m/z calcd for C20H23O
([M-H]+) 279.1749, obsd 279.1756.
