$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 1-Phenyl-3-(phenylselanyl)prop-2-yn-1-ol (7a),
Typical Procedure. A THF (2.0 ml) solution of phenylselanylethyne (0.60
g, 3.31 mmol) was added dropwise to a THF (8.0 ml) solution of LDA
(prepared from n-BuLi (1.80 ml, 3.97 mmol) and diisopropylamine (0.67 g,
3.32 mmol) at 0 °C. After stirring for 10 min, a THF (2.0 ml) solution of
benzaldehyde (0.70 g, 6.62 mmol) was added to a mixture. The whole was
poured into water (50 ml) and the organic layer was separated and the
aqueous layer was extracted with ether. The combined organic layer was
dried over MgSO4. The solvent was removed under reduced pressure. The
residue was purified by preparative TLC on silica gel eluting with
AcOEt-n hexane (1:10) to give 7a (0.78 g, 83%) as a pale yellow oil.
3-(Phenylselanyl)-1-(2-thienyl)prop-2-yn-1-ol (7h): Yield 88%, Yellow
oil, IR n 3290 (OH), 2172, 1577, 1476, 1439, 1290, 1228, 1169, 1022, 960,
852, 736, 706, 687; 1H NMR (600 MHz, CDCl3) δ 2.73 (1H, brs, OH), 5.83
(1H, d, J=10 Hz, CHO), 6.96 (1H, dd, J=3 and 5 Hz, ArH), 7.17 (1H, t, J=4
Hz, ArH), 7.25-7.31 (5H, m, ArH), 7.54 (1H, dd, J=1 and 4 Hz, ArH); 13C
NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 61.20 (d), 67.40 (s), 102.19 (s), 125.67 (d),
126.12 (d), 126.76 (d), 127.31 (d), 127.92 (s), 129.35 (dx2), 129.55
(dx2), 144.06 (s); MS m/z 294 (M+), 277 (M+-OH), 137 (M+-SePh). Anal.
Calcd for C13H10OSSe: C, 53.25; H, 3.44. Found: C, 53.24; H, 3.20.
