$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Electrophilic allylation with Allyl Chlorides
(general procedure B). The corresponding electrophile (0.25 mmol),
catalyst 1 (0.90 mg, 0.0025 mmol) and catalyst 2 (3.1 mg, 0.005 mmol)
were dissolved in THF (1.25 ml) containing 4Å molecular sieves (70 mg).
After addition of the corresponding allyl chloride (0.30 mmol), the
reaction mixture was stirred for 10 min, followed by addition of (SnMe3)2
(98 mg, 0.30 mmol). The reaction mixture was then stirred for the
allotted times and temperatures (Table 1). After evaporation of the
solvent the crude product was purified by silica gel chromatography. The
NMR spectra of products 5f-h and 5j are identical with those reported in
the literature.3 5g, yield 96%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, mol. sieves used
