$DATUM 109-99-9
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure A: Grignard Addition to an
Aldehyde: Grignard Reagent (2.0 eq.) was added dropwise to a stirred
solution of aldehyde (1.0 eq.) in THF (10 mL per 1.00 mmol substrate) at
-30 °C and the resulting solution was stirred at this temperature for 3
h. A saturated, aqueous solution of NH4Cl was added and the aqueous phase
was extracted with ethyl acetate (3 x 30 mL). The combined organic
extracts were washed with brine (30 mL), dried over MgSO4, filtered and
concentrated to give the crude product, which was then purified as
specified. 1-(4-Methoxypyridin-2-yl)but-3-en-1-ol, 8 as an oil, yield
0.510 g, 2.85 mmol, 79%. Rf 0.34 (ethyl acetate); IR νmax (thin
film/cm-1) 3207 (O-H), 1601 (C=C); 1H NMR δH (400 MHz, CDCl3) 8.36 (1 H,
d, J 5.8, NCH), 6.83 (1 H, d, J 2.3, C(CHOH)CH), 6.74 (1 H, dd, J 5.8,
2.3, NCHCH), 5.85 (1 H, ddt, J 17.4, 10.3, 7.0, CH=CH2), 5.15-5.10 (2 H,
m, CH=CH2), 4.76 (1 H, dd, J 7.3, 4.7, CHOH), 3.86 (3 H, s, OCH3), 3.84
(1 H, br s, OH), 2.67-2.60 (1 H, m, CH(OH)CHAHB), 2.51-2.44 (1 H, m,
CH(OH)CHAHB); 13C NMR δC (100 MHz, CDCl3) 166.3 (COMe), 163.5 (CCHOH),
149.5 (NCH), 134.2 (CH=CH2), 118.0 (CH=CH2), 108.9 (NCHCH), 105.9
(C(CH(OH))CH), 72.3 (CHOH), 55.2 (OCH3), 42.9 (CH(OH)CH2); MS m/z (ESI+)
180 (60%, M+H+), 202 (100%, M+Na+); HRMS (ESI+) C10H13NO2 requires M+H+
180.1019, found 180.1019 (+0.1 ppm).
