$DATUM (Z)-1,2-Diphenyl-1-hydroxy-4-methyl-3-trifluoromethylhex-4-ene (4c). A
solution of enol ether 3 (220 mg, 1 mmol), sec-butyllithium (1.6 mL of a
1.5 M solution in hexanes, 2.1 mmol), and TMEDA (490 mg, 2.1 mmol) in
hexane (10 mL), after addition of benzaldehyde (132 mg, 1.2 mmol),
afforded, after workup and purification, the alcohol 4c (298 mg, 88%). IR
(CCl4) 3660, 1632 cm-1; 19F NMR δ- 52.0 (s); 1H NMR δ 0.71/0.74 (t, J=
7.4 Hz, 3 H), 1.0/1.02 (d, J= 7.8 Hz, d, J= 8.3 Hz, 3H), 1.31 (m, 1 H),
1.53 (m, 1 H), 2.0 (m, OH), 2.2 (m, 1H), 6.1 (s, CHOH), 6.9-7.4 (m, 10
H); 13C NMR δ 12.5, 18.6/18.7, 27.2/27.3, 38.3/38.4, 71.4 (q, 4 JCF = 3.5
Hz), 125.4 (q, 1 JCF = 280 Hz), 125.9, 127.2, 127.8, 129.3, 133.4 (q, 2
JCF = 25 Hz), 135.4/135.5, 140.3, 148.9.(m, CCF3). Anal. Calc for
C20H21F3O : C 71.86, H 6.29. Found: C 71.75, H 6.42.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Short stereoselective route to γ-CF3 allylic alcohols: rearrangements
with creation of quaternary CF3-substituted carbons
