$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure II. Catalytic Asymmetric
Additions of tert-Butyl isocyanide A solution of tert-butyl isocyanide
(1.2 equiv, 1.0 M in CH2Cl2) was added to a solution of an aldehyde (1.0
M in CH2Cl2 based on aldehyde), chiral catalyst (0.05 equiv or 0.1
equiv), SiCl4 (1.1 equiv), and diisopropylethylamine (0.1 equiv) at -74
°C over the indicated time via a syringe pump. After being stirred for
the indicated time, the reaction mixture was transferred dropwise to a
vigorously stirred, ice-cold, saturated aqueous solution of NaHCO3 (20
mL). The mixture was stirred for 2 h at rt. The white precipitate was
filtered off through Celite and the filtrate was extracted with CH2Cl2 (4
x 20 mL). The combined organic layers were dried (MgSO4) and concentrated
under reduced pressure. The catalyst was separated from the product by
silica gel chromatography (hexane/EtOAc). Analytically pure product was
obtained after sublimation or recrystallization (heptane/benzene).
Following General Procedure II, a solution of tert-butyl isocyanide (125
μL, d = 0.735, 1.2 mmol, 1.2 equiv) in CH2Cl2 (1.0 mL) was added via a
syringe pump to the cold solution of (E)-2-methyl -cinnamaldehyde 3h (140
μL, d = 1.047, 1.0 mmol), catalyst (R,R)-1b (43 mg, 0.05 mmol, 0.05
equiv), SiCl4 (125 μL, d = 1.483, 1.1 mmol, 1.1 equiv), and
diisopropylethylamine (18 μL, d = 0.742, 0.1 mmol, 0.1 equiv) in CH2Cl2
(1.0 mL) at -74 °C over 4 h. The mixture was stirred further for 4 h at
-74 °C. After work-up and silica gel chromatography (20 mm column, 60 g
SiO2, Rf 0.28, hexane/EtOAc, 3/1), 212 mg (86%) of 53h was obtained as a
white solid. The enantiomeric ratio was determined to be 67.4/32.6,
(S)-5h/(R)-5h. Analytically pure sample (165 mg, 67%), which has an
enantiomeric ratio of 59.4/40.6, (S)-5h/(R)-5h, was obtained after
recrystallization from a 4/1 mixture of heptane and benzene . Data for
(S)-5h: mp: 112-113°C (heptane/benzene, 4/1) SFC: (S)-5h, tR 7.27 min
(67.4%); (R)-5h, tR 7.97 min (32.6%) (Chiracel AD, 4.5% MeOH in CO2, 125
bar, 40 °C, 2.5 mL min-1 ) (before recrystallization) SFC: (S)-5h, tR
7.22 min (59.4%); (R)-5h, tR 7.93 min (40.6%) (Chiracel AD, 4.5% MeOH in
CO2, 125 bar, 40 °C, 2.5 mL min-1 ) (after recrystallization) Analysis:
C15H21NO2 (247.33) Calcd: C, 72.84; H, 8.56; N, 5.66% Found: C, 72.80; H,
8.61; N, 5.80%
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, 67:33 enantiomeric ratio
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Catalytic, Enantioselective α-Additions of Isocyanides: Lewis Base
Catalyzed Passerini-Type Reactions
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Denmark, Scott E.; Fan, Yu
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2005), 70(24), 9667-9676

