$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure I. Pyridine N-Oxide
Catalyzed Additions of tert-Butyl isocyanide A solution of tert-butyl
isocyanide (1.2 equiv, 1.0 M in CH2Cl2) was added to a solution of an
aldehyde (1.0 M in CH2Cl2 based on aldehyde), pyridine N-oxide (0.1
equiv), and SiCl4 (1.1 equiv) at -74 °C over 30 min via a syringe pump.
After being stirred for the indicated time, the reaction mixture was
warmed to rt and transferred dropwise to a vigorously stirred, ice-cold,
saturated aqueous solution of NaHCO3 (20 mL). The mixture was further
stirred for 2 h at rt. The white precipitate was filtered off through
Celite and the filtrate was extracted with CH2Cl2 (4 x 20 mL). The
combined organic layers were dried (MgSO4) and concentrated under reduced
pressure. Pyridine N-oxide was separated from the product by silica gel
chromatography (hexane/EtOAc). Analytically pure product was obtained
after recrystallization (heptane/benzene).
N-tert-Butyl-2-hydroxy-3-methyl-4-phenyl-3-butenamide ((±)-5h) Following
General Procedure I, a mixture of (E)-2-methyl-cinnamaldehyde 3h (140 μL,
d = 1.047, 1.0 mmol), pyridine N-oxide (9.5 mg, 0.1 mmol, 0.1 equiv),
SiCl4 (125 μL, d = 1.483, 1.1 mmol, 1.1 equiv), and tert-butyl isocyanide
(125 μL, d = 0.735, 1.2 mmol, 1.2 equiv) in CH2Cl2 (2.0 mL) was stirred
for 4 h at -74 °C. After work-up and silica gel chromatography (20 mm
column, 60 g SiO2, Rf 0.28, hexane/EtOAc, 3/1), 211 mg (86%) of (±)-5h
was obtained as a white solid. White crystals of (±)-5h (185 mg, 75%)
were obtained after recrystallization from a 4/1 mixture of heptane and
benzene. Data for (±)-5h: mp: 125.5-126.0°C (heptane/benzene, 4/1) 1H
NMR: (400 MHz, CDCl3) 7.25-7.41 (m, 5 H, aryl); 6.62 (s, 1 H, HC(4));
5.78 (bs, 1 H, NH); 4.48 (d, J = 3.4, 1 H, HC(2)); 3.89 (d, J = 3.2, 1 H
, OH); 1.83 (s, 3 H, H3C(5')); 1.39 (s, 9 H, 3 X H3C(2'')) 13C NMR: (100
MHz, CDCl3) 170.9 (C(1)), 137.2 (C(1') or C(3)), 136.6 (C(1') or C(3)),
130.6 (C(4)), 128.9 (C(3')), 129.0 (C(2')), 127.1 ((C(4')), 77.8 (C(2)),
51.6 (C(1'')), 28.7 C(2'')), 12.2 (C(5'')) IR: (CHCl3) 3411 (s), 3010
(s), 2971 (s), 2935 (m), 2912 (m), 2873 (m), 1678 (s), 1523 (s), 1492
(m), 1456 (s), 1393 (s), 1367 (s), 1274 (s), 1232 (s), 1178 (m), 1083
(s), 1016 (s), 950 (m), 919 (m) TLC: Rf 0.28 (hexane/EtOAc, 3/1) SFC:
(S)-5h, tR 7.24 min (49.8%); (R)-5h, tR 7.95 min (50.2%) (Chiracel AD,
4.5% MeOH in CO2, 125 bar, 40 °C, 2.5 mL min-1) MS: (FI, 70 eV) 248 (15),
247 (100) Analysis: C15H21NO2 (247.33) Calcd: C, 72.84; H, 8.56; N, 5.66%
Found: C, 72.83; H, 8.67; N, 5.88%
