$DATUM 7732-18-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 1.1. General procedure for the synthesis of
hydroxy sulfinyl dienes. A round-bottomed flask was charged with THF (3.5
mL/mmol) and 2.6 equiv of freshly distilled i-Pr2NH, and cooled to -78
ºC. To the above solution was added 2.5 equiv of n-BuLi and the resulting
LDA solution (ca. 0.3 M) was stirred at this temperature. After 10 min a
solution of 1 equiv of a Z/E mixture of dienyl sulfoxides in THF (2
mL/mmol), previously dried over 4 Å sieves, was added dropwise slowly
(ca. 8 min/mmol of sulfoxide) to produce a pale yellow solution. After
stirring for an additional 10 min at -78 ºC, 3-5 equiv of freshly
distilled aldehyde was added dropwise and the resulting colorless
solution was stirred at this temperature for 10 min. The reaction mixture
was quenched with a saturated solution of NH4Cl (2 mL/mmol) and H2O (2
mL/mmol), diluted with EtOAc (3 mL/mmol) and the layers were separated.
The aqueous layer was extracted with EtOAc (3 times, 4 mL/mmol). The
combined organic extracts were washed with a saturated solution of NaCl
(4 mL/mmol), dried over MgSO4 and concentrated under reduced pressure to
give a crude product that was purified by column chromatography using the
appropriate mixture of eluents. 1.1.1. Synthesis of (+)-(1R,2E,SS
)-1-Naphtyl-2-(p-tolylsulfinyl)penta-2,4-dien-1-ol, 2b, and (-)-(1S,2E,SS
)-1-Naphtyl-2-(p-tolylsulfinyl)penta-2,4-dien-1-ol, 3b. From a solution
of the mixture of sulfinyl dienes 1E/Z (0.153 g, 0.80 mmol) in 6 mL of
THF, 2.5 equiv of LDA and 1-naphthaldehyde (0.324 mL, 0.373 g, 2.39
mmol), following the general procedure, a 45:55 mixture of hydroxy
sulfinyl dienes 2b and 3b was obtained. Chromatographic purification
(5-20% Et2O-CH2Cl2). 1.1.2. Synthesis of (+)-(1R,2E,SS
)-4-Methyl-1-phenyl-2-(p-tolylsulfinyl)penta-2,4-dien-1-ol, 2d, and
(-)-(1S,2E,SS )-4-Methyl-1-phenyl-2-(p-tolylsulfinyl)penta-2,4-dien-1-ol,
3d. From a solution of the mixture of sulfinyl dienes 1’Z/E (441 mg,
2.138 mmol) in 16 mL of THF, 2.5 equiv of LDA and benzaldehyde (0.65 mL,
680 mg, 6.41 mmol), following the general procedure. 23:77 mixture of
hydroxy sulfinyl dienes 2d and 3d was obtained. Chromatographic
purification (5-20% Et2O-CH2Cl2), gave 2d (143 mg, 21%) and 3d (477 mg,
71%) as colorless oils. 2d: Rf = 0.51 (20% Et2O-CH2Cl2). [α]20 D = +113.2
(c = 1.21). 1 H NMR (400 MHz), COSY δ 1.89 (s, 3 H, CH3), 2.34 (s, 3 H,
CH3 p-Tol), 2.87 (dd, 1 H, J = 6.6, 0.8 Hz, OH), 5.16-5.18 (m, 2 H,
H-5cis + H-5trans), 6.03 (d, 1 H, J = 6.6 Hz, H-1), 7.06 (s, 1 H, H-3),
7.15 (d, 2 H, J = 7.9 Hz, p-Tol), 7.17-7.22 (m, 5 H, Ph), 7.37 (d, 2 H, J
= 8.2 Hz, p-Tol). 13 C NMR (100 MHz), HSQC δ 21.4 (CH3 p-Tol), 22.5
(CH3), 70.6 (C-1), 120.2 (C-5), 125.4 (2 x p-Tol), 126.0 (2 x p-Tol),
127.3 (Ph), 128.1 (2 x Ph), 129.7 (2 x Ph), 135.9 (C-3), 139.0 (C-4),
140.5 (Ar), 140.7 (Ar), 141.5 (Ar), 145.8 (C-2). IR (film): 3325, 3085,
3060, 2975, 1621, 1596, 1493, 1449, 1081, 1010, 918, 810, 751, 736, 699
cm-1. HRMS (ES): calcd for C19H21O2S [M+H]+ 313.1262, found 313.1267. 3d:
Rf = 0.37 (20% Et2O-CH2Cl2). [α]20 D = -51.8 (c = 2.03). 1H NMR (400
MHz), COSY δ 1.78 (s, 3 H, CH3), 2.34 (s, 3 H, CH3 p-Tol), 3.75 (d, 1 H,
J = 6.9 Hz, OH), 5.08 (s, 2 H, H-5cis + H-5trans), 5.94 (d, 1 H, J = 6.8
Hz, H-1), 6.71 (s, 1 H, H-3), 7.16-7.19 (m 7 H, p-Tol + Ph), 7.40 (d, 2
H, J = 8.2 Hz, p-Tol). 13C NMR (100 MHz), HSQC δ 21.4 (CH3 p-Tol), 22.4
(CH3), 70.9 (C-1), 120.1 (C-5), 125.7 (2 x p-Tol), 126.2 (2 x p-Tol),
127.2 (Ph), 128.1 (2 x Ph), 129.8 (2 x Ph), 135.3 (C-3), 139.1 (C-4),
140.1 (Ar), 140.8 (Ar), 141.7 (Ar), 146.7 (C-2). IR (film): 3369, 3055,
2981, 1632, 1596, 1493, 1450, 1265, 1081, 1025, 1011, 906, 809, 736, 700
