$DATUM 1-(3,5-Bis(tert-butyldimethylsilyloxy)phenyl)but-3-en-1-ol (5). To a
solution of 4 (20.0 g, 54.5 mmol) in THF (340 mL) at 0 °C was added
allylmagnesiumbromide (48.2 mL of a 1.7 M solution in THF, 81.9 mmol)
dropwise via syringe over 30 minutes. The solution was allowed to stir
for 30 minutes at 0 °C and subsequently allowed to warm to room
temperature and stir for 3 hours. The reaction was quenched with a
saturated solution of NH4Cl in water. The aqueous solution was extracted
with ether (3 × 50 mL), dried (Na2SO4), and concentrated. 5 as colorless
oil (22.1 g, 99%) after purification (SiO2, 3% EtOAc/Hexanes). 1H (400
MHz, CDCl3): δ 6.46 (d, J = 2.2 Hz, 2H), 6.24 (t, J = 2.2 Hz, 1H),
5.78-5.72 (m, 1H), 5.14-5.06 (m, 2H), 4.63-4.60 (m, 1H), 2.47-2.43 (m,
2H), 2.01 (br s, 1H), 0.95 (s, 18H), 0.18 (s, 12H); 13C (100 MHz, CDCl3):
δ 156.3, 145.9, 134.1, 118.0, 110.9, 110.7, 72.9, 43.5, 25.5, 20.5, -0.7;
HRMS: calculated mass = 408.2516 (M+H), observed mass = 408.2550 (M+H);
IR (CHCl3, cm-1): 3454, 2937, 2886, 1589, 1405, 1331, 1254, 1163.
