$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1-(5-((tert-Butyldimethylsilyloxy)methyl)furan-2-yl)but-3-en-1-ol (rac.
8): A solution of aldehyde 4 (7.50 g, 31.2 mmol) in THF (100 mL) was
stirred in an ice bath. To this solution was added slowly allyl magnesium
bromide (37 mL, 1.0 M in THF, 1.2 equiv) through a cannula. After the
completion of the reaction as judged by TLC (ca 30 min), saturated
solution of NH4Cl (100 mL) was added to the mixture and stirred
vigorously. When clear, the organic layer was separated. The aqueous
layer was washed with EtOAc (3 x 20 mL). The combined organic layers were
dried over Na2SO4 and concentrated. The crude product was chromatographed
(10% EtOAc/hexanes) to give 7.00 g oil (79% yield). IR (film) νmax/cm-1
3390, 2930, 2858, 1694, 1643, 1472, 1464, 1256, 1080, 1019, 837, 779. 1H
NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 6.17 (q, J = 3.3 Hz, 2H), 5.87-5.76(m, 1 H),
5.21-5.14(m, 2H), 4.72(dd, J = 12.4 Hz, 5.2 Hz, 1 H), 4.62(s, 1 H),
2.65-2.59 (m, 2H), 2.01(d, J = 4.8 Hz, 1 H), 0.90(s, 9 H), 0.08(s, 6 H).
13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 155.5, 153.8, 133.7, 118.5, 107.8, 106.7,
67.0, 58.1, 40.0, 25.8, 18.3, -5.27.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
