$DATUM 7732-18-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: A general procedure for the stereoselective
construction of β-hydroxyallenes via the reaction of
α-alkenyl-zirconacyclopentenes with aldehydes. To a solution of Cp2ZrCl2
(0.183 g, 0.625 mmol) in THF (5 mL) was added EtMgBr (1.0 M THF solution,
1.25 mmol) at ca. -50 °C. After stirring for 1 h at the same temperature,
(E)-enyne (0.5 mmol) was added and the reaction mixture was warmed up to
room temperature and stirred for 2 h. Aldehyde (0.5 mmol) was added and
the mixture was stirred at room temperature for 3-6 h.The reaction
mixture was quenched with 3N HCl and extracted with ethyl acetate. In the
case of the reaction with 4-(dimethylamino)benzaldehyde, the reaction
mixture was quenched with water. The extract was washed with water, brine
and dried over Na2SO4. The solvent was evaporated in vacuo and the
residue was purified by chromatography on silica gel to afford β
-hydroxyallene derivative 5. (1R*, 2S*,
R*a)-5-Ethyl-2-phenyl-1-thien-2-yl-deca-3,4-dien-1-ol (5g). Purification
by flash chromatography on silica-gel (eluent: petroleum ether: EtOAc:
Et3N = 94: 5: 1) afforded the title compound in 76% isolated yield. 1H
NMR (CDCl3, Me4Si) δ 0.83 (t, J = 6.9 Hz, 3H), 1.00 (t, J = 7.5 Hz, 3H),
1.19-1.34 (m, 6H), 1.90-2.01 (m, 4H), 2.81 (bs, 1H), 3.60 (dd, J = 8.1,
7.5 Hz, 1H), 5.14 (d, J = 7.8 Hz, 1H), 5.48-5.53 (m, 1H), 6.59 (d, J =
3.6 Hz, 1H), 6.78 (dd, J = 3.3, 3.6 Hz, 1H), 7.12-7.25 (m, 6H); 13C NMR
(CDCl3, Me4Si) δ 12.3, 14.0, 22.4, 25.6, 27.2, 31.5, 32.6, 55.8, 73.9,
92.6, 108.4, 124.2, 124.4, 126.1, 126.6, 128.2, 128.3, 140.9, 145.6,
201.3. HRMS (EI) calcd for C22H28OS 340.1861, found 340.1854.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, regioselective, stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Stereoselective Synthesis of β-Hydroxyallenes with Multiple Contiguous
Stereogenic Centers via Aldehyde Addition to α-Alkenyl-Substituted
Zirconacyclopentenes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Zhou, Yebing; Chen, Jingjin; Zhao, Chunbin; Wang, Erjuan; Liu, Yuanhong;
Li, Yuxue
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2009), 74(15), 5326-5330

