$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the synthesis of
β-thioalkoxy alcohols 2 and 8. At -78 °C, under N2 atmosphere, to a THF
solution of product (1.00 equiv) was added dropwise nBuLi (1.10 equiv,
2.5 M hexane solution). After stirring at this temperature for 1 h, a THF
solution of carbonyl compound (1.00 equiv) was then added dropwise. The
mixture was gradually warmed to rt and stirred for 2-8 h, quenched with
sat. NH4Cl, washed with brine and extracted with ether. The organic layer
was dried (MgSO4), filtered and the filtrate was evaporated in vacuo to
give the residue which was chromatographed on silica gel (hexane/ethyl
acetate = 15-20/1) to give product as a pale-yellow liquid, yield 2.10 g,
88%.
7-Butyl-7-(1-hydroxyl-3-phenylprop-2E-enyl)-8,11-dithiapentadec-5-yne as
a pale-yellow liquid, yield 2.11 g, 81%. 1H NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz): δ
0.80-0.98 (m, 9 H), 1.22-1.65 (m, 14 H), 2.20-2.35 (m, 2 H), 2.49 (t, J =
7.5 Hz, 2 H), 2.62-2.76 (m, 3 H), 2.80-3.02 (m, 2 H), 4.12-4.22 (m, 1 H),
6.45 (dd, J = 15.9, 5.8 Hz, 1 H), 6.68 (d, J = 15.9 Hz, 1 H), 7.20-7.45
(m, 5 H); HRMS (FAB+) (M+1) calcd for C26H41O2S2: 433.2599, found:
433.2592. Characteristic 1H NMR data for minor isomer: 2.75 (t, J = 7.5
Hz, 2 H), 4.25-4.32 (m, 1 H), 6.37 (dd, J = 15.9, 5.8 Hz, 1 H), 6.73 (d,
J = 15.9, Hz, 1 H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Iron-Promoted Elimination of β-Thioalkoxy Alcohols. Olefination by
Coupling of a Carbonyl Group with a Dithioacetal
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
