$DATUM The starting (S,S)-bis-sulfonamide ligand (220 mg, 0.42 mmol) was dried
under high vacuum at 120 °C overnight then cooled down to rt and
dissolved in CH2Cl2 (4.0 mL). The solution was cooled to 0 °C and boron
tribromide (0.43 mL, 0.43 mmol, 1.0 M solution in CH2Cl2) was added. The
resulting mixture was stirred at 0 °C for an additional 10 min and then
warmed to rt. Stirring was continued at rt for 1 h and solvent was then
removed under high vacuum. The residue was re-dissolved in CH2Cl2 (2.0
mL) and was then removed under high vacuum again. The residue was
dissolved in CH2Cl2 (1.5 mL) and the resulting solution was cooled to 0
°C. A solution of 2-bromo-3-(tri-n-butylstannyl)-1-propene (198 mg, 0.48
mmol) in CH2Cl2 (1.0 mL) was added. The resulting mixture was warmed to
rt and stirred for an additional 12 h. The gold solution was then cooled
to -78 °C and a solution of the aldehyde 14 (117.8 mg, 0.31 mmol) in
CH2Cl2 (2.0 mL) was introduced via syringe. The resulting mixture was
stirred at -78 °C for an additional 2 h. The reaction was quenched by
addition of pH 7 buffer (2.5 mL). The mixture was warmed to rt and poured
into a solution of potassium fluoride (5.0 mL, 2.0 N aq). The resulting
mixture was stirred at rt for 30 min and two layers were separated. The
organic layer was collected and the aqueous phase was extracted with Et2O
(30 mL x 3). The combined organic layers were washed with pH 7 buffer (30
mL x 2) and brine (100 mL) respectively. The solution was dried over
sodium sulphate and concentrated in vacuo. The crude product was purified
with flash silica gel column chromatography (hexanes:EtOAc = 6:1) to
provide the allylation product 25. Colorless oil, yield 127.4 mg, 0.26
mmol, 82% (dr greater than 95:5). Rf = 0.25 (hexanes:EtOAc = 5:1); [α]D22
-57.7 (c 1.02, CHCl3); IR (thin film, cm-1): 3454, 3071, 2958, 2929,
2857, 1689, 1642, 1462, 1427, 1378, 1206, 1112, 1008; 1H NMR (400 MHz,
CDCl3) δ (ppm): 7.70 - 7.68 (m, 4H), 7.46 - 7.38 (m, 6H), 5.68 (s, 1H),
5.49 (s, 1H), 5.06 (d, J = 10.4 Hz, 1H), 4.81 (m, 1H), 3.57 (dd, J = 9.6,
6.0 Hz, 1H), 3.47 (dd, J = 9.6, 6.8 Hz, 1H), 2.80 - 2.77 (m, 1H), 2.75 -
2.69 (m, 1H), 2.57 - 2.53 (dd, J = 15.0, 5.0 Hz, 1H), 2.27 (d, J = 2.0
Hz, 1H), 1.79 (s, 3H), 1.64 - 1.57 (m, 1H), 1.24 - 1.17 (m, 1H), 1.08 (s,
9H), 0.92 (t, J = 7.2 Hz, 3H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ (ppm): 137.6,
135.9, 135.8, 133.7, 130.9, 130.6, 129.8, 127.8, 119.4, 69.0, 67.6, 48.0,
41.9, 27.0, 24.8, 19.4, 12.0; HRMS-ESI (calc. for C27H37O2SiBrNa [M+Na]+)
523.1644, found 523.1653.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, agent dependent stereochemistry, in-situ generated
reactant in stage 2, buffered solution used in stage 4
