$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for enantioselective Henry
reaction A solution of amino pyridine 4 (6.7 mg, 0.025 mmol) in methanol
(1.5 mL) was added to Cu(OTf)2 (9.0 mg, 0.025 mmol) contained in a
Schlenk tube under nitrogen. The mixture was stirred for 1 h at rt until
the formation of a green solution. Then, the aldehyde 1 (0.25 mmol) was
added and the reaction flask introduced in a bath at the reaction
temperature. After 5 min, methyl 4-nitrobutyrate (2, 318 μL, 2.5 mmol)
was added followed by Et3N (35μL, 0.25 mmol) and the reaction mixture was
stirred until completion (TLC). The mixture was treated with 1M aqueous
HCl (15 mL) and extracted with dichloromethane (3 × 15 mL). The organic
layer was washed with brine (20 mL), dried over MgSO4 and concentrated
under reduced pressure. Finally unreacted methyl 4-nitrobutyrate was
removed by distillation at reduced pressure in a Kugelrohr. The products
3 in the distillation flask. Methyl 5-hydroxy-4-nitro-5-phenylpentanoate
(3a)2 Purified according to the general procedure. Diastereomeric ratios
(anti/syn, 85:15) were determined by 1H NMR. Enantiomeric excesses were
determined by chiral HPLC (Chiralpak AS-H), hexane:i-PrOH 90:10, 1
mL/min. (E)-Methyl 5-hydroxy-4-nitro-7-phenylhept-6-enoate (3j) Purified
according to the general procedure. Diastereomeric ratios (anti/syn,
74:26) were determined by 1H NMR. Enantiomeric excesses were determined
by chiral HPLC (Chiralpak IC), hexane:i-PrOH 90:10, 1 mL/min. Anti isomer
(4R,5S): (ee 91%); Syn isomer (4S,5S): (ee 62%). anti major(4R,5S)
tr=19.0, anti minor(4S,5R) tr=26.6, syn major(4S,5S) tr=37.2, syn
minor(4R,5R) tr=34.4. Anti isomer (4R,5S): [α]D 25 +6.0 (c 0.58, CHCl3);
1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.41-7.28 (5H, m), 6.75 (1H, dd, J = 15.9, 1.2
Hz), 6.17 (1H, dd, J = 15.9, 6.0 Hz), 4.81-4.77 (1H, m), 4.74-4.69 (1H,
m), 3.68 (3H, s), 2.82 (1H, br s), 2.56-2.22 (4H, m); 13C NMR (75.5 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 172.6 (C), 135.6 (C), 134.2 (CH), 128.7 (CH), 128.5 (CH), 126.8
(CH), 124.9 (CH), 90.3 (CH), 73.1 (CH), 51.9 (CH3), 29.9 (CH2), 23.4
(CH2); Syn isomer (4S,5S): [α]D 25 –21.0 (c 0.24, CHCl3); 1H NMR (300
MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.42-7.29 (5H, m), 6.76 (1H, d, J = 15.9 Hz), 6.13 (1H, dd,
J = 15.9, 7.2 Hz), 4.73-4.65 (2H, m), 3.69 (3H, s), 2.82 (1H, br s),
2.45-2.13 (4H, m); 13C NMR (75.5 MHz, CDCl3) δ 172.2 (C), 135.4 (C),
135.1 (CH), 128.7 (CH), 128.6 (CH), 126.8 (CH), 125.0 (CH), 91.2 (CH),
73.9 (CH), 52.0 (CH3), 29.7 (CH2), 25.4 (CH2); MS (EI) m/z (%): 261
[(M+-H2O), 0.2], 133 (100), 131 (82), 91 (72), 55 (91); HRMS: 261.1010
(M+– H2O), C14H15NO4 required 261.1001.
