$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
5-Methyl-4-phenyl-1-pyridin-3-yl-4,7-octadien-1-yn-3-ol (4c); This
reaction was carried General Procedure B. To a solution of 1-alkyne (2.00
mmol) in THF (2 mL) was added n-BuLi (1.5 M solution in n-pentane, 2.00
mmol) at -78 °C. After 30 min, dienal 10 (2.00 mmol) was added to the
mixture. The mixture was stirred for 30 min at the same temperature and
then quenched by addition of water. After extraction three times with
EtOAc, the combined organic layers were dried over Na2SO4 and
concentrated under reduced pressure. The residue was purified by silica
gel flash column chromatography to give 4,7-octadien-1-yn-3-ol 4.
1-(3-Chloropropyl)-5-(4-methoxyphenyl)-4-methyl-4,7-octadien-1-yn-3-ol
(4f); This reaction was carried out according to the General Procedure B;
purified by silica gel flash column chromatography (hexane/EtOAc = 2/1)
(92% yield). 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ 1.73 (s, 3H), 1.95-2.01 (m, 3H), 2.45 (td,
J = 6.7, 1.9 Hz, 2H), 3.14 (ddd, J = 15.8, 6.3, 0.6 Hz, 1H), 3.21 (ddd, J
= 15.9, 5.8, 0.7 Hz, 1H), 3.65 (t, J = 6.4 Hz, 2H), 3.81 (s, 3H), 5.00
(dq, J = 10.2, 1.8 Hz, 1H), 5.04 (dq, J = 17.1, 1.9 Hz, 1H), 5.42 (br s,
1H), 5.77 (ddt, J = 17.1, 10.4, 5.8 Hz, 1H), 6.84-6.87 (m, 2H), 7.06-7.09
(m, 2H); 13C NMR (CDCl3) δ 14.55, 16.22, 31.23, 38.49, 43.57, 55.15,
62.20, 80.93, 83.77, 113.36, 115.53, 129.58, 132.03, 135.01, 135.33,
135.67, 158.13; HRMS (FAB) calcd for C19H22ClO (M+-OH) 301.1359, found
301.1369.
