$DATUM (S)-Alcohol 20: Aldehyde 9 (2.0 g, 7.24 mmol) was subjected to Keck's
catalytic asymmetric allylation conditions to afford 1.83 g (79%, 94% ee)
of the title alcohol.5 The optical purity of this material was
established by removal of the tosylate and formation of the benzyl
protected alcohol.6 Data for alcohol 20: [α]23 D -22.0 (c 0.75, CH2Cl2);
IR (neat) 3542-3408 (br), 2926, 1598, 1502, 1370 cm-1; 1H NMR (400 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 7.69 (d, J = 8.2 Hz, 2 H), 7.31 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 2 H), 7.28 (d, J
= 8.6 Hz, 2 H), 6.95 (d, J = 8.5, 2 H), 5.80-5.70 (m, 1 H), 5.19-5.10 (m,
2 H), 4.75-4.67 (m, 1 H), 2.50-2.38 (m, 2 H and s, 3 H), 2.15 (d, J = 2.9
Hz, 1 H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 148.7, 145.3, 142.7, 133.9, 129.7,
129.2, 128.4, 127.0, 122.3, 118.9, 72.4, 43.9, 21.7; HRMS m / z calcd for
C17H17O3S [M - OH]+ 301.0898, found 301.0906.
