$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Methyl 3-(2-furyl)-3-hydroxy-2-methylenepropanoate (18c). Purification by
column chromatography (4:1 hexane/EtOAc) afforded a desired compound 18c
(156 mg, 86%) as a pale-yellow liquid. Spectral data were identical to
those previously reported.4 TLC: R f 0.46 (2:1 hexane/EtOAc). 1H NMR (400
MHz, CDCl3): δ 7.38 (m, 1H), 6.39 (s, 1H), 6.34 (dd, 1H, J = 3.2, 2.0
Hz), 6.27 (d, 1H, J = 3.2 Hz), 5.94 (s, 1H), 5.59 (d, 1H, J = 6.4 Hz),
3.77 (s, 3H), 3.05 (d, 1H, J = 6.4 Hz). 13C-NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ
166.7, 154.3, 142.6, 139.6, 127.1, 110.6, 107.4, 67.7, 52.3. LRMS (FAB)
m/z (rel int): 165 ([M-OH]+, 100), 182 ([M], 10), 205 ([M+Na]+, 10). HRMS
m/z calcd for C9H10O4 182.0579 found 182.0574.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Baylis-Hillman reaction, 1-butyl-3-methyltriazolium triflimide as solvent
gave lower yield
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
