$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):SOL(2):CAS_RN
$DATUM 110-54-3
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Procedure A: Formation of alcohols via allyl indium reagents s-Butyl
lithium (1.0 M solution in hexanes, 3.0 eq.) was added to a stirred
solution of allyl ethyl ether (3.0 eq.) in THF (10 mL/mmol) at -78 °C.
After stirring for 1 h, a solution of InCl3 (1.0 eq.) in THF (5 mL/mmol)
was added. Stirring was continued for a further 30 min before addition of
the corresponding aldehyde (1.0 eq.). After 1 h, the reaction mixture was
allowed to warm to room temperature before addition of 1.0 M aq. HCl
solution (5 mL/mmol). The aqueous layer was extracted with Et2O (10
mL/mmol × 2) and the combined organic layers were washed with water
(10mL/mmol) and sat. aq. NaCl solution (10 mL/mmol) and dried over
Na2SO4. The solvent was removed under reduced pressure, and the crude
product was purified by flash column chromatography to give the
corresponding alcohol as a mixture of diastereoisomers which were not
separated. (1RS,2RS) and
(1RS,2SR)-1-(4-Bromophenyl)-2-ethoxybut-3-en-1-ol 6a 4-Bromobenzaldehyde
(186 mg, 1.00 mmol) was subjected to general procedure A and purified by
flash column chromatography (10:1 petrol:Et2O) to give alcohol 6a as a
colourless oil (190 mg, 70%) and a mixture of diastereoisomers (ca. 2:1
from 1H NMR) which were not separated. The 1H and 13C NMR data provided
is for the major diastereoisomer. νmax (thin film)/cm-1 3448br s, 3060s,
2976s, 2929s, 1488s, 1401s, 1071s, 930s, 823s; δH (400.2 MHz, CDCl3) 1.22
(3H, t, J 7.0, C(2')H3), 3.32-3.42 (2H, m, C(1')H2), 3.60-3.68 (2H, m,
C(2)H, OH), 4.44 (1H, d, J 8.0, C(1)H), 5.01-5.08 (1H, m, C(4)H),
