$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Cyclohex-1-eneacetylene (1.90 g, 18.0 mmol) was dissolved in 10 mL of dry
THF and cooled to -78 °C and at that temperature slowly n-BuLi (7.2 mL,
2.5 M in THF) was added to the reaction mixture. The reaction mixture was
then warmed to -40 °C over a period of 4 h and again cooled to -78 °C.
Then at that temperature salicyaldehyde (1.0 g, 8.19 mmol) was added
dropwise to the reaction mixture. The reaction mixture was then stirred
for 12 h maintaining the same temperature until the disappearance of the
starting material. Then the reaction mixture was quenched by the addition
of saturated NH4Cl and extracted with DCM, dried over anhydrous Na2SO4
and concentrated to obtain the crude product which was finally purified
by column chromatography (25-50% EtOAc/Hexane). Isolate 1.42 g (76%) of
1m.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Directing Group Assisted Nucleophilic Substitution of Propargylic
Alcohols via o-Quinone Methide Intermediates: Bronsted Acid Catalyzed,
Highly Enantio- and Diastereoselective Synthesis of
7-Alkynyl-12a-acetamido-Substituted Benzoxanthenes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Saha, Satyajit; Schneider, Christoph
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
