$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Preparation of
Compounds 24 and 26-30. To a stirred solution of appropriate aldehyde
(1.00 mmol) in THF (2 mL), acrylonitrile (197 μL, 3.00 mmol), MeOH (2
mL), and water (4 mL) were added. DABCO (112 mg, 1.00 mmol) was then
added to the mixture, and the reaction was allowed to stir at room
temperature until TLC showed complete or stable consumption of the
aldehyde (23-166 h). The mixture was diluted with CH2Cl2 (3 × 25 mL) and
washed with water (25 mL) and brine (30 mL), dried (Na2SO4), and the
solvent evaporated under reduced pressure. The crude product was purified
by FC as indicated. 2-(Hydroxy(naphthalen-1-yl)methyl) acrylonitrile
(28). The product was obtained using 1-naphthaldehyde in 7 days. The
crude product was purified by FC eluting with PE/EtOAc from 9/1 to 8/2 to
afford 28 as a yellowish oil (0.720 mmol, 150.7 mg, 72% yield). MS/CI
(isobutane): [M-H]+ 210; 1H NMR (CDCl3): δ, 7.91-7.68 (m, 3H, ArH),
7.56-7.20 (m, 4H, ArH), 5.83 (d, 2H, J = 1.1 Hz, C═CH2), 5.67 (s, 1H,
CH), 3.83 (s, 1H, OH); 13C NMR (CDCl3): δ, 137.8, 134.9, 134.5, 131.6,
130.4, 129.8, 129.2, 129.1, 128.0, 127.5, 127.4, 125.2, 118.4, 75.9.
cLogP: 2.62. TC50: 10.1 ± 2.5.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM combinatorial, Morita-Baylis-Hillman reaction
