$DATUM 3-Hydroxy-2-methylene-3-(4-nitrophenyl)propanenitrile (19e). Purification
by column chromatography (3:1 hexane/EtOAc) afforded a desired compound
19e (198 mg, 97%) as a pale-yellow crystal. Spectral data were identical
to those previously reported.8 TLC: R f 0.38 (1:1 hexane/EtOAc). mp: 72.1
°C (Lit.,6: 72-75 °C). 1H-NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 8.28 (d, 2H, J = 8.8
Hz), 7.62 (d, 2H, J = 8.8 Hz), 6.20 (d, 1H, J = 1.6 Hz), 6.12 (d, 1H, J =
1.6 Hz), 5.46 (d, 1H, J = 4.0 Hz), 2.52 (d, 1H, J = 4.0 Hz). 13C-NMR (100
MHz, CDCl3): δ 148.4, 146.0, 131.1, 127.6, 125.6, 124.3, 116.4, 73.6.
