$DATUM 7732-18-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM To a stirred solution of 4-nitrobenzylaldehyde (0.302 g, 2 mmol), aqueous
trimethylamine (0.5 mL, 2.5 mmol) in methanol (2 mL) was added
acrylonitrile (0.40 mL, 6 mmol). The resulting clear mixture was stirred
at room temperature for 0.5h (monitored by TLC). Then chloroform (20 mL)
and water (5 mL) were added and the mixture was stirred for another 2
min. The organic phase was separated and the water phase was extracted
with chloroform (2 x10 mL). The combined organic phase was dried over
anhydrous magnesium sulfate. After removing of the solvent and low
bolting-point substance the crude product was purified by column
chromatography to afford the pure adduct. (1a), as a pale yellow solid.
Yield 85%. m.p. 72~75°C. 1H NMR(δ, CDCl3): 2.11(br., OH), 5.44(s, 1H),
6.10(s, 1H), 6.18(1s, 1H), 7.60(d, 2H), 8.26(d, 2H). Anal. Calculated for
C10H8N2O3: C, 58.82; H, 3.95; N, 13.72. Found: C, 59.01; H, 4.03; N,
13.51.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Dramatic Rate Acceleration of the Baylis-Hillman Reaction in Homogeneous
Medium in the Presence of Water
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Cai, Juexiao; Zhou, Zhenghong; Zhao, Guofeng; Tang, Chuchi
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2002), 4(26), 4723-4725

