$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 3-Hydroxy-2-methylene-3-(4-trifluoromethylphenyl)propanenitrile (19j).
Purification by column chromatography (3:1 hexane/EtOAc) afforded a
desired compound 19j (212 mg, 93%) as a pale-yellow liquid. Spectral data
were identical to those previously reported.12 TLC: R f 0.24 (3:1
hexane/EtOAc). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 7.68 (d, 2H, J = 8.4 Hz), 7.55
(d, 2H, J = 8.4 Hz), 6.16 (d, 1H, J = 1.2 Hz), 6.09 (d, 1H, J = 1.2 Hz),
5.41 (m, 1H), 2.39 (brs, 1H). 13C-NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ 143.1, 131.2
(q, JCF = 32.4 Hz), 130.8, 127.0, 126.1 (q, JCF = 3.8 Hz), 125.9, 124.1
(q, JCF = 270.5 Hz), 116.7, 73.7.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Baylis-Hillman reaction, 1-butyl-3-methyltriazolium hexafluorophosphate
as solvent gave lower yield
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of 1,3-Dialkyl-1,2,3-triazolium Ionic Liquids and Their
Applications to the Baylis-Hillman Reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Jeong, Yunkyung; Ryu, Jae-Sang
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2010), 75(12), 4183-4191

