$DATUM 1-(3-phenoxyphenyl)prop-2-en-1-ol (2f) Aldehyde (10 mmol) was added
dropwise to a 1 M solution of the Grignard reagent (11 mmol, 11 mL) in
THF, at 0 °C. After stirring for 2 h at 0 °C, saturated aq. NH4Cl
solution (100 mL) was added. The aqueous layer was extracted three times
with AcOEt. The combined organic extracts were dried over Na2SO4, and
solvent was evaporated to produce alcohol, which was used in the next
reaction without further purification. 1-(3-phenoxyphenyl)prop-2-en-1-ol
(2f) 2.0 g, yield 88%, yellow oil. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 7.40-7.30
(m, 3H), 7.16-7.10 (m, 2H), 7.10-7.08 (m, 1H), 7.06-7.02 (m, 2H), 6.94
(ddd, J = 8.1, 2.6, 1.1 Hz, 1H), 6.03 (ddd, J = 17.1, 10.5, 6.2 Hz, 1H),
5.34 (dt, J = 17.1, 1.4 Hz, 1H), 5.20 (dt, J = 10.5, 1.4 Hz, 1H), 5.16
(br d, J = 6.2 Hz, 1H), 2.61 (br s, 1H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ
157.5, 157.1, 144.8, 140.0, 129.9, 129.8, 123.3, 121.1, 118.9, 118.0,
116.8, 115.5, 75.0; HRMS-ESI: m/z 249.0886 ([M+Na]+, C15H14NaO2 calcd.
m/z: 249.0897).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Building Molecular Complexity via Tandem Ru-catalyzed Isomerization/C-H
Activation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Bartoszewicz, Agnieszka; Martin-Matute, Belen
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
