$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1-(3-Bromophenyl)-2-(triisopropylsilyl)prop-2-en-1-ol (1i) A flame-dried
25 mL flask was charged with (1-bromovinyl)triisopropylsilane (S3) (527
mg, 2 mmol) and filled with argon. 10 mL of THF was added and the
solution was cooled to -78 °C. Butyllihium solution (1.6 M in hexanes,
1.25 mL, 2 mmol) was added dropwise. The mixture was left stirring at -78
°C for 1 h. A separate flame-dried argon-filled 25 mL flask was charged
with m-bromobenzaldehyde (277 mg, 1.5 mmol) and 5 mL of THF and the
solution was cooled to -78 °C. The organolithium compound solution was
slowly (~2 drops/s) cannulated to the stirred aldehyde solution; the
solution was then left at -78 °C for 30 min. 3 mL of methanol were added
at once, the mixture was quickly allowed to room temperature; water was
added and the products were extracted with dichloromethane. The combined
extracts were dried over anhydrous sodium sulfate and concentrated. The
residue was purified by column chromatography on silica gel in 1:40 ethyl
acetate - hexanes system to give the product. Colorless oil, yield 399
mg, 72%. 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.52 (s, 1H), 7.40 (d, J = 7.9 Hz,
1H), 7.28 (d, J = 7.7 Hz, 1H), 7.20 (t, J = 7.8 Hz, 1H), 6.02 (t, J = 1.6
Hz, 1H), 5.63 (d, J = 1.9 Hz, 1H), 5.34 (d, J = 4.0 Hz, 1H), 1.84 (d, J =
4.2 Hz, 1H), 1.17 (sep, J = 7.4 Hz, 3H), 1.04 (d, J = 7.4 Hz, 9H), 0.95
(d, J = 7.4 Hz, 9H); 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ 149.1, 144.8, 130.6,
129.8, 128.7, 126.1, 122.4, 76.0, 18.6, 18.5, 11.2; For [MNa]+
C18H29BrNaOSi calculated 391.1069, found (TOF MS ES+) 391.1072; FTIR
(film, NaCl) νmax 3396 (m), 3061 (w), 2944 (s), 2890 (m), 2866 (s), 1593
(w), 1570 (w), 1465 (m), 1427 (m), 1406 (m), 1383 (m), 1367 cm-1 (m).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM intermediate from stage 1 added in stage 2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Formation of Five- and Seven-Membered Rings Enabled by the
Triisopropylsilyl Auxiliary Group
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Usanov, Dmitry L.; Yamamoto, Hisashi
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2012), 14(1), 414-417

