$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Representative procedure for the preparation
of the allylic alcohols 1a-c:1 5-Phenylpent-1-en-3-ol (1a).
1-(2,4-Dimethoxyphenyl)prop-2-en-1-ol (1c). This product was prepared
from 3,5-dimethoxybenzaldehyde (1.2 g, 7.5 mmol) according to the general
procedure to afford the desired compound as a pale yellow oil in
quantitative yield (1.5 g, 7.5 mmol). The crude compound was used without
any further purification. An analytical sample was purified by silica gel
chromatography (elution with EtOAc/hexane 10:90) to obtain the following
spectroscopic data which corresponds to that reported in the literature.4
1H-NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.19 (d, J = 9.0 Hz, 1H), 6.48-6.45 (m, 2H),
6.11 (ddd, J = 17.2, 10.4, 5.5 Hz, 1H), 5.36 (br t, J = 5.7 Hz, 1H), 5.29
(dt, J = 17.2, 1.6 Hz, 1H), 5.15 (dt, J = 10.4, 1.5 Hz, 1H), 3.83 (s,
3H), 3.80 (s, 3H), 2.58 (d, J = 5.9 Hz, 1H); 13C-NMR (125.8 MHz, CDCl3) δ
160.6, 158.0, 139.9, 128.3, 123.6, 114.1, 104.5, 99.1, 71.2, 55.6, 55.5;
IR (neat) 3423, 2938, 2836, 1611, 1588, 1504, 1464, 1292, 1262 cm-1; HRMS
(ES-) m/z calcd. for C11H13O3 (M-H)- 193.0865, found 193.0844.
